  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "For the consent-based condition described in the Manual, the trade mark owner must agree to an endorsement recording consent from the Plant Breeder’s Rights (PBR) titleholder.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/1/2-1-2-c-letter-of-consent",
          "quote": "In this circumstance, the owner of the trade mark will need to agree to an endorsement to that effect."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual’s example condition requires the applicant to have the PBR titleholder’s consent to use the variety name or synonym in a trade mark for the duration of the PBR right.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/1/2-1-2-c-letter-of-consent",
          "quote": "It is a condition of registration that the applicant has the consent of the PBR titleholder to use the <plant variety name/synonym> ‘xxxx’ in a trade mark for the duration of the PBR right."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "In that consent-based arrangement, the Manual also requires the registered goods to be restricted to accord with the plant variety name or synonym.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/1/2-1-2-c-letter-of-consent",
          "quote": "The goods will also need to be restricted to accord with the plant variety name or synonym."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/1/2-1-2-c-letter-of-consent",
          "quote": "<Specification>; all the foregoing being plants or plant material of <genus> < variety name/synonym ‘xxxx’>"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Separately, the Manual explains that, in use, the trade mark needs to be clearly differentiated from the variety name rather than used instead of it.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/3/2-3-1-c-trade-names-and-alternate-names~1",
          "quote": "However, both agree that trade marks in use need to be clearly differentiated from the variety name and not used instead of it."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual identifies acceptable presentation formats as placing the trade designation before the genus/variety information or otherwise clearly separating it from that information.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/3/2-3-1-c-trade-names-and-alternate-names~1",
          "quote": "Acceptable formats for trade mark purposes are where the trade designation precedes the genus/variety information or is otherwise clearly separated from it."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The supplied passages do not establish who else is legally bound by a registration condition—for example, authorised users or later owners—or the consequences of breach; the exact condition and further legislative provisions would be needed to answer that part.",
